# No em dashes

Do not use the em dash character (U+2014) in code, UI copy, docs, emails, comments, commit messages, or chat replies.

Use a regular hyphen-minus (`-`) instead.

```text
Bad:  Start Your Journey [em dash] 14 Day Free Trial
Good: Start Your Journey - 14 Day Free Trial

Bad:  Hard days need recovery [em dash] not another chore
Good: Hard days need recovery - not another chore

Bad:  return "[em dash]"
Good: return "-"
```

Prefer ASCII hyphens for ranges and labels too when writing new copy (`1-5`, `A-Z`, `SKU - Title`). Do not introduce en dashes (U+2013) as a substitute for em dashes.
